**Rationale for the changes:**

| Concern | How it is addressed |
|---|---|
| Bulk-safe loading | `OpportunitiesSelector.selectById` uses a single SOQL via fflib's `selectSObjectsById`. |
| Skip already-Closed-Won | Filter loop before mutation; count reflects only newly closed records. |
| Single UoW / single commit | One `Application.UnitOfWork.newInstance()` handles both the DML (`registerDirty`) and the event publishing (`registerPublish`). `commit()` is called exactly once. |
| Events only after successful DML | fflib's `SObjectUnitOfWork.doCommit` performs DML first; `registerPublish` events are queued and only published *after* the DML succeeds. A thrown exception aborts the entire UoW—no events go out—and propagates to the caller. |
| Platform-event type registered | `Deal_Won__e.SObjectType` is added to the `UnitOfWorkFactory` list so fflib recognises and can publish that event type through its UoW pipeline. |
| Null / empty input | Early-return `0` before any query. |

I kept your approach. I only added defensive guards (null/empty/duplicate IDs), skipped DML when there is nothing to update, and handled an unexpected empty error list. I did not reject normalized values that are empty or contain non-leading `+`, because your stated rule is to keep digits and `+`.

