for (OpportunityLineItem line : lines) {
    if (line.Discount == null) {
        line.Discount = discounts.get(line.Product2Id);
    }
}
```

Until `PricingRules` offers a batch path, the per-line call works correctly for small inserts but **will fail at scale**. A short-term mitigation on our side (without touching the pricing class) would be to cache results in a static `Map<Id, Decimal>` inside the handler keyed on `Product2Id`, so duplicate products across the 200 lines only pay one SOQL each—useful but not a full fix if all 200 product IDs are distinct.

**Other minor points handled in the code above:**

| Concern | What I did |
|---|---|
| Null / empty `Trigger.new` | Early-return guard |
| `Product2Id` unexpectedly null | Skipped (no discount applied) rather than NPE |
| `Discount` of `0` vs `null` | Only `null` triggers the lookup; an explicit `0` is preserved |
| Trigger pattern | Thin trigger delegates entirely to the handler (per Salesforce best practice, easy to toggle/disable) |
| Sharing | `with sharing` on both classes, consistent with `PricingRules` |

